{#
    Gotenberg renders this as its own document in the bottom margin of every page, filling the
    pageNumber and totalPages spans. It cannot load the rider's font, so it uses the system sans
    serif with inline styles. It is one line on purpose: this context ignores width, so flexbox, a
    table or a float to push the page number to the right all collapse onto the text.

    The band and the rider are named here rather than in a running header: page 1 already opens on
    them, and a header cannot be left off the first page. Numbers are only printed when the rider is
    one render: Gotenberg numbers each render on its own, so after a merged attachment they would
    restart at 1.
#}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="fr">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <style>
        body { margin: 0 14mm; font-family: sans-serif; font-size: 7.5pt; color: #6b7280; }
        .line { padding-bottom: 5mm; }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="line">
    {{ band_name }} · {{ rider_name }} · édité le {{ generated_at }}{% if numbered %} · page <span class="pageNumber"></span> / <span class="totalPages"></span>{% endif %}
</div>
</body>
</html>
